# Build context for the single-container image (the root `Dockerfile`).
#
# The root Dockerfile builds the web app in a `node:22-alpine` stage, runs
# `npm ci`, and then does `COPY frontend/ ./`. Without this file that `COPY`
# carries the developer's `node_modules` (713 MB) and `.next` (345 MB) into
# the stage and lays them over the install the container just made — so the
# image ships the host's dependency tree, built for the host's libc, instead
# of the lockfile's for Alpine's musl. See `frontend/.dockerignore` for the
# same problem in the other direction.
#
# It also keeps the context from carrying the whole working tree.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Nothing in the image is built from these.
docs
android
api
assets
scripts
uploads

# Host-installed dependencies and build output, at any depth.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage

# Local state: the SQLite database, the uploads directory, virtualenvs.
backend/data
backend/.venv
backend/uploads
worker/.venv
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
